{#-
  The shell every page of the site is built into. A page supplies its own <main> and nothing else:
  the doctype, the head, the stylesheet links and the closing tags are written once, here.

  Front matter a page may set:
    title       the page's name. "interesting" is appended, so index.html leaves it out.
    description the <meta name='description'>, omitted when absent.
    stylesheet  a name in css/: "diary" links css/diary.css after the shared css/site.css, so the
                page's own rules win over the shared ones. Omit it for a page that needs none.
    inlineStyles
                write the styles into the page instead of linking them. Only error.html needs it:
                CloudFront returns that page for any 404, at whatever path was asked for, so a
                relative <link> next to it would be a guess.
    footer      the links the page ends with, as [href, text] pairs (see footer.njk).
    footerNote  an aside shown after those links.

  Three shared lines are written here rather than in every page, which is the whole point of a
  shared shell: each axiom is about the built site, so one line here carries it to all of them.
    js/analytics.js  the Google Analytics tag and the consent banner that gates it (see
                     ANALYTICS_TAG and check_analytics in .github/scripts/make_interesting.py).
    js/state.js      the one local-state document every page reads and writes through, and the
                     meta menu that exports it (STATE_TAG and check_state).
    js/threshold.js  the mood flow: the site ascertains a visitor's orientation before it offers
                     them anything, and keeps asking, in a new way, on every page (MOOD_TAG and
                     check_mood).
  None of the three may be dropped: a built page missing any of them is refused. The files behind
  the first two are fixed; js/threshold.js is protected instead, so a run may rewrite the flow but
  never delete it.

  The mood ribbon below is the flow made visible. It sits outside <main> on every page, so the
  question is never a gate in front of the content: the whole site is reachable with the ribbon
  ignored, or with scripting switched off entirely.

  Links are relative, like every link in the site: it has no fixed domain and may be served under
  a sub-path, so "css/site.css" and not "/css/site.css".
-#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang='en'>
<head>
  <meta charset='utf-8'>
  <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1'>
  <title>{% if title %}{{ title }} · {% endif %}interesting</title>
{%- if description %}
  <meta name='description' content='{{ description }}'>
{%- endif %}
{%- if inlineStyles %}
  <style>{{ 'site' | css | safe }}{{ stylesheet | css | safe }}</style>
{%- else %}
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='css/site.css'>
{%- if stylesheet %}
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='css/{{ stylesheet }}.css'>
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
  <!-- Analytics and the cookie consent banner that gates it; see js/analytics.js. -->
  <script src='js/analytics.js' defer></script>
  <!-- The one local-state store every page reads and writes through, and its meta menu; see
       js/state.js. Not deferred: a page's own script runs before any deferred one does. -->
  <script src='js/state.js'></script>
  <!-- The mood flow: ask before offering, on every page; see js/threshold.js. Deferred, and so
       after js/state.js, which is what it keeps its reading in. -->
  <script src='js/threshold.js' defer></script>
  <script src='js/site.js' defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a class='skip-link' href='#main-content'>skip to main content</a>
  <header class='site-header'>
    <p class='site-header-title'>
      <a href='index.html'>interesting</a>
      <span>many worlds, no default</span>
    </p>
    <p class='site-meta' aria-live='polite'>
      <span id='site-pulse-status' class='site-meta-status'>sky pulse: checking shared constellation memory...</span>
      <a id='site-pulse-link' class='site-meta-link' href='index.html'>open home constellation</a>
    </p>
    <nav class='site-header-nav' aria-label='Primary navigation'>
      <a href='index.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'index' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>threshold</a>
      <a href='moods.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'moods' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>mood atlas</a>
      <a href='sitemap.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'sitemap' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>site map</a>
      <a href='error.html'{% if page and page.fileSlug == 'error' %} aria-current='page'{% endif %}>404</a>
    </nav>
  </header>
  <aside class='mood-ribbon' id='mood-ribbon' data-asking='false' aria-label='What this site has read about you'>
    <p class='mood-ribbon-text' id='mood-ribbon-text'>Nothing read yet.</p>
    <p class='mood-ribbon-where' id='mood-ribbon-where'>reading the clock and the zone…</p>
    <div class='mood-ribbon-actions'>
      <button type='button' id='mood-ribbon-ask' aria-expanded='false' aria-controls='mood-probe'>ask me another way</button>
      <a class='action' id='mood-ribbon-go' href='moods.html' hidden>go to your world</a>
      <a class='action' href='moods.html'>mood atlas</a>
    </div>
    <div class='mood-probe' id='mood-probe' hidden></div>
  </aside>
  <div id='main-content' tabindex='-1'>{{ content | safe }}</div>
</body>
</html>
